USE THIS ONE. Of the three patches over this file, a human should apply exactly
this one:
  * grader-quarantine.patch       (1a alone) — settlement quarantine only
  * grader-stale-feed.patch       (1b alone) — stale-feed quarantine only
  * grader-quarantine-stale.patch (BOTH)     — this file
1a and 1b conflict textually: both rewrite the helper block before connect(),
the fetch_directional_days SQL and the fetch_calibration_bins SQL, and both add
a key at the same JSON payload anchor. 1a also aliases the outcome table as
`po`, which the 1b predicate must reference. Applying 1a and then 1b (or the
reverse) will fail; this file is the merged result, built by applying 1a to a
clean checkout, layering 1b on top, and diffing against HEAD.

WHAT IT DOES
  1a — excludes any resolved outcome row whose label was frozen BEFORE its
       forward bar's session had closed (the resolver graded a partial bar).
       Structural, per row, reconstructed from the bar stamps.
  1b — excludes any graded (symbol, horizon, trading-day) observation minted on
       a day the daemon had already flagged that SYMBOL's own feed stale
       (dq_events kind='stale', written by internal/maintain's DQAuditor).
  The two filters are independent and compose: 1b's published count is
  MARGINAL, i.e. what it removes from the population 1a already trimmed.

  Nothing is written and nothing is relabelled by either filter.

